"To solve the equation \\((3^k)^6 = 3^6\\), we can use the properties of exponents. Specifically, we will use the property \\((a^m)^n = a^{mn}\\).\n\nStep 1: Apply the property of exponents to the left side of the equation.\n\\[\n(3^k)^6 = 3^{k \\cdot 6}\n\\]\nSo the equation becomes:\n\\[\n3^{k \\cdot 6} = 3^6\n\\]\n\nStep 2: Since the bases are the same, we can set the exponents equal to each other.\n\\[\nk \\cdot 6 = 6\n\\]\n\nStep 3: Solve for \\(k\\) by dividing both sides of the equation by 6.\n\\[\nk = \\frac{6}{6} = 1\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(k\\) is \\(\\boxed{1}\\)."
