"To solve the equation \\(\\log_5(x-18) = 2\\), we need to convert the logarithmic equation to its exponential form. The exponential form of a logarithmic equation \\(\\log_b(a) = c\\) is \\(b^c = a\\).\n\nGiven:\n\\[\n\\log_5(x-18) = 2\n\\]\n\nWe can rewrite this in exponential form as:\n\\[\n5^2 = x - 18\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\(5^2\\):\n\\[\n5^2 = 25\n\\]\n\nSo, the equation becomes:\n\\[\n25 = x - 18\n\\]\n\nTo solve for \\(x\\), we add 18 to both sides of the equation:\n\\[\n25 + 18 = x\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx = 43\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(x\\) is \\boxed{43}.\n\\]"
