"We start with the given system of equations:\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\nx + y - z &= -8, \\\\\nx - y + z &= 18, \\\\\n-x + y + z &= 30.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nFirst, we add all three equations together:\n\\[\n(x + y - z) + (x - y + z) + (-x + y + z) = -8 + 18 + 30.\n\\]\nSimplifying the left-hand side, we get:\n\\[\n2x + 2y + 2z = 40.\n\\]\nDividing both sides by 2, we find:\n\\[\nx + y + z = 20.\n\\]\n\nNext, we subtract the second equation from this result:\n\\[\n(x + y + z) - (x - y + z) = 20 - 18.\n\\]\nSimplifying, we get:\n\\[\n2y = 2,\n\\]\n\\[\ny = 1.\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(xyz\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1}.\n\\]"
"To find the slope of a line perpendicular to the line given by the equation \\(\\frac{x}{4} - \\frac{y}{5} = 1\\), we first need to determine the slope of the given line.\n\nThe given equation is in the form \\(y = mx + b\\), where \\(m\\) is the slope. We can rewrite the given equation in this form:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{x}{4} - \\frac{y}{5} = 1\n\\]\n\nMultiply every term by 20 to clear the denominators:\n\n\\[\n5x - 4y = 20\n\\]\n\nRearrange to solve for \\(y\\):\n\n\\[\ny = \\frac{5}{4}x - 5\n\\]\n\nThe slope \\(m\\) of the given line is \\(\\frac{5}{4}\\).\n\nThe slope of a line perpendicular to another line is the negative reciprocal of the original of the original line. Therefore, the slope of the perpendicular line is:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\nm = -\\frac{4}{5}\n\\]\n\nThus, the slope of the perpendicular line is \\(\\boxed{-\\frac{4}{5}}\\)."
