"To find the sum of all the odd integers between 500 and 700, we can use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series. The first term of this sequence is 501, and the last term is 699. The common difference between consecutive terms is 2.\n\nFirst, we need to determine the number of terms in this sequence. The number of terms can be found by dividing the difference between the last term and the first term by the common difference and then adding 1:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Number of terms} = \\left((699 - 501) \\div 2\\right) + 1 = 49\n\\]\n\nNext, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Sum} = \\frac{\\text{Number of terms} \\times (\\text{First term} + \\text{Last term})}{2} = \\frac{49 \\times (501 + 699)}{2} = \\frac{49 \\times 1200}{2}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= \\boxed{29400}\n\\]"
