"Let's denote the value of a triangle as \\( T \\) and the value of a circle as \\( C \\).\n\nFrom the given equations, we have:\n\\[\n1T + \\bigcirc + 1T + \\bigcirc + 1T + \\bigcirc + 1T + 1T = 21\n\\]\n\\[\n\\bigcirc + 1T + \\bigcirc + 1T + \\bigcirc + 1T + \\bigcirc + \\bigcirc = 16\n\\]\n\nSimplifying these equations:\n\\[\n7T + 5C = 21\n\\]\n\\[\n5T + 7C = 16\n\\]\n\nWe can solve this system of linear equations. First, let's simplify the second equation by subtracting the first equation from it:\n\\[\n(5T + 7C) - (7T + 5C) = 16 - 21\n\\]\n\\[\n5T + 7C - 7T - 5C = -5\n\\]\n\\[\n-2C = -5\n\\]\n\nThus, the sum of two circles is \\(\\boxed{-5}\\)."
