"We start with the given equation:\n\\[ 2ab = 12 \\]\n\nFirst, we need to express \\(8a^2b^2\\) in terms of \\(2ab\\). Notice that:\n\\[ 8a^2b^2 = (2ab)^2 \\cdot (2ab) \\]\n\nWe know that:\n\\[ 2ab = 12 \\]\n\nSo, we can substitute \\(2ab\\) with 12:\n\\[ 8a^2b^2 = (2ab)^2 \\cdot 12 \\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\((2ab)^2\\):\n\\[ (2ab)^2 = 12^2 = 144 \\]\n\nNow, we multiply this result by 12:\n\\[ 8a^2b^2 = 144 \\cdot 12 \\]\n\nFinally, we perform the multiplication:\n\\[ 144 \\cdot 12 = 1728 \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(8a^2b^2\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1728}\n\\]"
