"To determine the total number of possible license plates, we need to consider the number of choices available for each position on the license plate.\n\n1. **Choosing the letters:**\n   - There are 26 letters in the English alphabet.\n   - Each license plate consists of 2 different letters.\n   - The number of ways to choose 2 different letters from 26 is \\( 26 \\times 25 = 650 \\).\n\n2. **Choosing the digits:**\n   - There are 10 digits (0 through9).\n   - Each license plate consists consists of 2 different digits.\n   - The number of ways to choose 2 different digits from 10 is \\( 10 \\times 9 = 90 \\).\n\n3. **Total number of license plates:**\n   - The total number of license plates is the product of the number of ways to choose the letters and the number of ways to choose the digits.\n   - This is \\( 650 \\times 90 = 58500 \\).\n\nTherefore, the total number of possible license plates is \\(\\boxed{58500}\\)."
