"First, we calculate the total number of ways to choose a President, Vice-President, and Treasurer from a group of 8 people without any restrictions. This is simply the number of permutations of 8 people taken 3 at a time, which is $8 \\times 7 \\times 6 = 336$.\n\nNext, we calculate the number of ways to choose a President, Vice-President, and Treasurer from a group of 4 guys and 4 girls such that no girl holds any of the positions. This is simply the number of permutations of 4 guys taken 3 at a time, which is $4 \\times 3 \\times 2 = 24$.\n\nTherefore, the number of ways to choose a President, Vice-President, and Treasurer from a group of 4 guys and 4 girls such that at least one girl and at least one guy holds at least one of those three positions is the total number of ways to choose the positions minus the number of ways to choose the positions with no girls.\n\nSo the answer is $336 - 24 = \\boxed{312}$.\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is $312$. I hope it is correct."
"The binomial coefficient $\\dbinom{10}{4}$ is calculated using the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{10}{4} = \\frac{10!}{4!(10-4)!} = \\frac{10!}{4! \\cdot 6!}\n\\]\n\nWe can simplify this by canceling out the common terms in the numerator and the denominator:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{10}{4} = \\frac{10 \\times 9 \\times 8 \\times 7 \\times 6!}{4! \\times 6!} = \\frac{10 \\times 9 \\times 8 \\times 7}{4!}\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate $4!$:\n\n\\[\n4! = 4 \\times 3 \\times 2 \\times 1 = 24\n\\]\n\nNow, we divide the product of the numerator by the denominator:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{10}{4} = \\frac{5040}{24} = 210\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is $\\boxed{210}$."
