"The projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$ is given by the formula:\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{a} = \\frac{\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}}{\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{b}\n\\]\nFirst, we need to calculate $\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}$:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = 2^2 + 6^2 + 3^2 = 4 + 36 + 9 = 49\n\\]\nNext, we use the given value $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = 8$:\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{a} = \\frac{8}{49} \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\nTherefore, the projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$ is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}}\n\\]\nFinal Answer: The final answer is $\\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}$. I hope it is correct."
